# Everything under .local/share/nvim is generated state, not configuration:
# mason's installed language servers, treesitter queries, telescope history,
# netrw history. mason and packer write ABSOLUTE symlinks into it
# (/home/piero/.local/share/nvim/mason/packages/...), and stow refuses an
# absolute symlink outright -- "source is an absolute symlink ... All
# operations aborted" -- which on a fresh machine aborted the whole stow
# invocation and, before df_stow_repo was guarded, the whole bootstrap run.
#
# None of it is worth carrying between machines: nvim's plugin manager
# rebuilds all of it on first launch, which phase_report already tells the
# operator to do. Wallpapers, the other half of this package, still stow.
^/\.local/share/nvim$
